  "snp2.14:5.1": "At <a href='https://suttacentral.net/dn20/en/sujato#11.7'>DN 20:11.7</a> Erāvaṇa is clearly a dragon, but later tradition depicted him as a great elephant, the mount of Sakka. ",
  "snp2.14:5.2": "",
  "snp2.14:5.3": "",
  "snp2.14:5.4": "",
  "snp2.14:6.1": "Kuvera is identified as Vessavaṇa at <a href='https://suttacentral.net/dn32/en/sujato#7.43'>DN 32:7.43</a>. ",
  "snp2.14:6.2": "",
  "snp2.14:6.3": "",
  "snp2.14:6.4": "",
  "snp2.14:7.1": "While <i lang='pi' translate='no'>titthiya</i> is commonly found in the Vinaya, this is the only place it occurs in the suttas that is not part of a stock list including kings, etc., or compounded with <i lang='pi' translate='no'>añña-</i> or <i lang='pi' translate='no'>nānā-</i>. ",
